</gallery>

==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
TEC (53).png|Enhanced Speed
SA (75).png|Enhanced Agility/Enhanced Reflexes
BT (197).png|Enhanced Strength
CR (47).png|Enhanced Durability
EoMF (103).png|Enhanced Jumping
SA (70.5).png|Enhanced Acrobatics
</gallery>
Fasttrack has enhanced speed, agility and reflexes. Fasttrack is able to run fast enough to outrun a missile created by [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]], forcing Animo to increase the power of the missile in an attempt to make it outspeed Fasttrack.<ref name="TEC">''[[The Eggman Cometh]]''</ref>

Fasttrack possesses enhanced strength, as he was able to carry both [[Hulka]] and [[Tack]] to safety,<ref>''[[Basic Training]]''</ref> as well as [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] while in [[Legerdomain]].<ref name="EoMF" />

Fasttrack possesses enhanced durability.<ref name="CR">''[[Couples Retreat]]''</ref><ref name="SA">''[[Solitary Alignment]]''</ref>

Fasttrack can jump to great heights while running,<ref name="EoMF" /> and is quite acrobatic, as while upside-down, he performed a handspring to avoid a swipe from [[Sir George]]; leap in the air; and realign himself before he touched the ground.<ref name="SA"/>

===Non-Canon Powers and Abilities===
====[[Ben 10: Galactic Racing|Galactic Racing]]====
[[File:SA6EG9-4.png|thumb|Fasttrack using "Spininjutsu"]]
Fasttrack can become intangible.{{Refn|[[:File:SA6EG9-4.png]]|group = GR|name = spin}}

Fasttrack is capable of creating fast-spinning tornadoes.{{Refn|group = GR|name = spin}}

Fasttrack can create fake copies of himself through "Spininjutsu".{{Refn|group = GR|name = spin}}

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
SA (62).png|Exploitable Speed
TEC (282).png|Poor Traction
TEC (55).png|Slippery Surfaces
</gallery>
Opponents with good reflexes and reaction time can counter Fasttrack's speed and land a blow on him, as seen when Fasttrack ran straight into [[Sir George]]'s outstretched arm, badly stunning him.<ref name="SA" /> 

Fasttrack can have a hard time stopping if he runs too quickly.<ref name="TEC" />

Being a speed-based alien, Fasttrack shares similar weaknesses with [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]]. For example, he is being unable to run on certain surfaces like ice, which can make him slip very easily.<ref name="TEC" />

==History==
===Ultimate Alien===
*Fasttrack first appeared and was unlocked off-screen in ''[[Basic Training]]'',{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: The Wild Truth]]''; [[:File:TWT Fasttrack Data.png|file]]|group = DVD}} where he saved [[Tack]] and [[Hulka]] from an explosion caused by a [[Nuclear Fusion Grenade]].
*In ''[[A Knight to Remember]]'', Fasttrack disarmed the [[Forever Knights]] by taking all of their weapons away.
*In ''[[Solitary Alignment]]'', Fasttrack tried to take the sword, [[Ascalon]], from [[Sir George]], but failed and was defeated by him, forcing Fasttrack to switch into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].
*In ''[[Enemy of My Frenemy]]'', Fasttrack was tied to [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] (with [[manna]]) so they could all escape from the [[Scrutin]]s together. He and [[Alien Force|the team]] then met [[Ignaceous]].
*In ''[[The Eggman Cometh]]'', Fasttrack trained with Kevin until they were stopped by Gwen. Later, Fasttrack failed to stop [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s missile from destroying a weather balloon experiment.
*In ''[[Couples Retreat]]'', Fasttrack failed to catch [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Darkstar]] and stop him from going to the [[Door to Anywhere]]. He then looked around for the stolen page from Gwen's [[Gwen's Spellbook|spellbook]] before reverting.
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', Fasttrack appeared twice in a dream. Firstly, [[Albedo|Negative]] Fasttrack fled from [[Swampfire]]. Seconds later, Ben as Fasttrack chased Negative Fasttrack all the way to [[Mr. Smoothy (Classic)|Mr. Smoothy]].
*In ''[[The Beginning of the End]]'', Fasttrack defeated the [[Esoterica]] who were spying on him, Gwen, and Kevin.

