==Etymology==
"Fast track" is an informal phrase meaning "the quickest and most direct route to achievement of a goal", as in competing for professional advancement.

==Trivia==
*Although Fasttrack did not appear in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', he was mentioned in ''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]'', ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]'', and ''[[Breakpoint]]''.
**There were no plans for Fasttrack to appear during the early seasons of the show.{{Refn|[[:File:Fasttrack Not Planned For Early OV Seasons.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Fasttrack and [[Eatle]] are the only aliens introduced in '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' to have been unlocked off-screen.
*Fasttrack's voice sounds very similar to [[Spidermonkey (Classic)|Spidermonkey]]'s.
*Fasttrack's name was first revealed in a ''[[Ben 10: Galactic Racing]]'' press release and confirmed by [[Peter David]], who revealed the name of Fasttrack's [[Citrakayah|species]] and [[Chalybeas|home planet]] as well.{{Refn|group = PAD|name = revelation}}
*Fasttrack was named by Peter David, albeit spelled as "Fasstrak".{{Refn|group = script|name = sa script}}
*Fasttrack was designed by [[Steven Choi]].{{Refn|[[:File:Steven Choi Designed Fasttrack.png]]|group = TJC}}
*Fasttrack's working names were Blustreek,{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/4/4a/A_Knight_to_Remember_DRAFT-1.pdf A Knight to Remember First Draft]|group = script}}{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/c/c1/TEC_Script_Outline_Second_Draft.pdf ''The Eggman Cometh'' Script Outline Second Draft]|group = outline}} Bluestreak{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/0/04/EoMF_Script_Outline_First_Draft.pdf ''Enemy of My Frenemy'' Script Outline First Draft]|group = outline}}{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/4/4a/A_Knight_to_Remember_DRAFT-1.pdf A Knight to Remember First Draft]|group = script}}{{Refn|[[:File:Beginning of the End OUTLINE.pdf]]|group = outline}} and SpeedFreak.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/36/Couples_Retreat_Draft-2.pdf ''Couples Retreat'' Script Second Draft]|group = script|name = script2}} Bluestreak was previously used as [[Jetray (Classic)|Jetray]]'s working name.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/23/Hero_Generation_Series_Bible.pdf Hero Generation Series Bible]|group = HG Bible|name = bible}}
*Fasttrack was originally not supposed to appear in:
**''[[Basic Training]]'', with Jetray taking his role.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/31/Basic_Training_Draft-1.pdf ''Basic Training'' Script First Draft]|group = script}}
**''[[Couples Retreat]]'', with [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]] taking his role.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/e/ef/Couples_Retreat_Draft-1.pdf ''Couples Retreat'' Script First Draft]|group = script}}
**The dream in ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]''.{{Refn|[https://web.archive.org/web/20250621100125/https://dwaynemcduffie.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/WEBSITE-B10UA-ep317-Night-of-the-Living-Nightmare-SCRIPT-D1.pdf ''Night of the Living Nightmare First Draft'']|group = script}}
*The reason why Fasttrack was absent in '''Omniverse''' was because the crew was unable to figure out how to make him more interesting compared to what was shown in '''Ultimate Alien'''.{{Refn|[[:File:Fasttrack Scrapped in OV Explanation.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Had he appeared, Fasttrack would have worn clothes, similar to many other aliens.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Fasttrack Would Have Worn Clothes.png]]|group = DJW}} [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] would have had [[Dee Bradley Baker]] reprise his role, but with some feline attributes added to his voice.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Fasttrack Voice.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Fasttrack might be able to be controlled by people who have the ability to control cats, like [[Nyancy Chan]], depending on how prevalent his feline attributes are.{{Refn|[[:File:Fasttrack Controlled By Nyancy.png]]|group = DJW}}
*A concept idea for Fasttrack's '''Omniverse''' design depicted him with wheeled feet inspired by the Wheelers from '''''[[Wikipedia:Return to Oz|Return to Oz]]'''''. However, it was rejected because the design made him look even more similar to [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]].{{Refn|[[:File:OV Fasttrack Wheelers Inspiration.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Derrick eventually drew a version of Fasttrack in the '''Omniverse''' art style, as well as an alternate version depicting him with sunglasses similar to [[Bullfrag]]'s, as part of a GoFundMe in 2021.{{Refn|https://www.gofundme.com/f/derrick-j-wyatt-draws-ov-fasttrack--more|group = DJW}} The alternate design was made after Derrick received several fan requests regarding Fasttrack wearing sunglasses.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Fasttrack Sunglasses Requested By Fans.png]]|group = DJW}}
**According to him, the Omnitrix was positioned on his chest because if it were on his belt, the symbol would need to be much smaller than normal and would still cover the end of the lightning bolt printed on his clothing.{{Refn|https://archive.vn/YRosu|group = DJW|name = DJW}}
**Derrick gave him a longer torso and thinner limbs, as he thought it would make him look more feline.{{Refn|group = DJW|name = DJW}}
**A version of him was also made with glasses similar to Bullfrag's. Derrick jokingly explained that Fasttrack wears running glasses because he doesn't want people to think he was crying when he shows up after a run, since the high speed combined with the exposure to the wind would make him tear up.{{Refn|group = DJW|name = DJW}}
*[[Matt Wayne]] speculates that Fasttrack is physically stronger than XLR8, stating that "Fasttrack can probably lift more".{{Refn|[[:File:Fasttrack Physically Stronger Than XLR8.PNG]]|group = MW}}

